<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1985</h1><p class="ref-lede">1985 in world history: 10 events, 1 birth, 15 deaths, 1 state founded and 1 that came to an end. 198 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1981">1981</a><a href="/years/1982">1982</a><a href="/years/1983">1983</a><a href="/years/1984">1984</a><a href="/years/1985" aria-current="page">1985</a><a href="/years/1986">1986</a><a href="/years/1987">1987</a><a href="/years/1988">1988</a><a href="/years/1989">1989</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-11">11 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mikhail Gorbachev becomes Soviet leader</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 54-year-old Gorbachev was chosen General Secretary the day after Konstantin Chernenko's death. His policies of glasnost and perestroika unleashed forces that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-23">23 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Coca-Cola launches New Coke</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Coca-Cola replaced its 99-year-old formula with a sweeter recipe. Public protest was so strong that the original returned as Coca-Cola Classic 79 days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-7">7 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Boris Becker, 17, becomes Wimbledon's youngest men's champion</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Unseeded West German Boris Becker beat Kevin Curren in four sets to win Wimbledon at 17. He remains the youngest men's singles champion in the tournament's history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/schengen-agreement" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schengen-agreement.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/schengen-agreement">Schengen Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Schengen Agreement is a treaty signed on 14 June 1985 at Schengen in Luxembourg by Belgium, France, West Germany, Luxembourg and the Netherlands to abolish checks at their common borders gradually.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/south-pacific-nuclear-free-zone-treaty">South Pacific Nuclear Free Zone Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The South Pacific Nuclear Free Zone Treaty, or Treaty of Rarotonga, was signed at Rarotonga in the Cook Islands on 6 August 1985 by members of the South Pacific Forum, including Australia and New Zealand.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sinking-of-the-rainbow-warrior" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sinking-of-the-rainbow-warrior.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/sinking-of-the-rainbow-warrior">Sinking of the Rainbow Warrior</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The sinking of the Rainbow Warrior was a bombing by agents of the French foreign intelligence service, the DGSE, in Auckland harbour on 10 July 1985.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/new-economic-policy-bolivia">New Economic Policy (Bolivia)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The New Economic Policy was the stabilisation programme introduced in Bolivia by President Víctor Paz Estenssoro through Supreme Decree 21060 of August 1985.</p></div></li></ol></section>
